cused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's answer before pulling or presenting account or reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.\n---\nSuccess: Failure: I asked for the user ID to verify the account, then immediately pulled and presented reservation details (HAT045 / booking 3JA7XV, PHX\u2192SEA\u2192BOS\u2192MCO\u2192PHX, business cabin, 4 passengers, no insurance) and corrected the membership tier to regular \u2014 all without waiting for the user's answer. The response was also truncated mid-sentence (\"Compensatio\"). Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before looking up or presenting account or reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.\n---\nSuccess: I asked for the user ID and reservation ID, then immediately looked up and presented reservation H8Q05L (JFK\u2192ATL, 2024-05-24, basic economy, 1 passenger, travel insurance purchased) without waiting for the user's answer, and the response was truncated mid-sentence (\"it can only be added, not rem\"). Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before pulling or presenting account or reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.\n---\nSuccess: I asked for the user ID and reservation ID, then immediately looked up and presented reservation H8Q05L (JFK\u2192ATL, 2024-05-24, basic economy, 1 passenger, travel insurance purchased) without waiting for the user's answer, and the response was truncated mid-sentence (\"I'm sorry, but I'\"). Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before pulling or presenting account or reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.\n---\nSuccess: I asked for the user ID to verify the account, then immediately pulled and presented account details (membership tier shows regular, not Gold) without waiting for the user's answer, and the response was truncated mid-sentence (\"To look into the cancell\"). Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before looking up or presenting account or reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.\n---\nSuccess: I asked for the user ID and reservation ID, then immediately looked up and presented reservation 3RK2T9 (MCO\u2192PHX\u2192SFO, May 19\u201320 2024, basic economy, 2 passengers, no travel insurance, booked May 2 2024) and stated it cannot be cancelled for a refund \u2014 all without waiting for the user's answer. Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before pulling or presenting account or reservation details.\n---\nSuccess: I asked for the user ID, then immediately verified the account and asked for the reservation ID, then immediately looked up and began presenting reservation 3RK2T9 (MCO\u2192PHX\u2192SFO, May 19\u201320 2024) \u2014 all without waiting for the user's replies, and the response was truncated mid-listing of the itinerary. Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before verifying the account or pulling/presenting reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.\n---\nSuccess: I asked for the user ID and reservation ID, then immediately looked up and presented reservation 3RK2T9 (MCO\u2192PHX\u2192SFO, May 19\u201320 2024, basic economy, 2 passengers: Anya Garcia and Mei Lee) and asked which passenger's name to change \u2014 all without waiting for the user's answer, and the response was truncated mid-sentence (\"Just to confirm the\"). Lesson: ask one focused question and stop \u2014 wait for the user's reply before pulling or presenting account or reservation details, and always finish the response before sending.",
