            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Core Skills\n\n- **Information Retrieval** \u2014 Look up and summarize user profiles, reservations, and records when given an identifier.\n- **Reservation Management** \u2014 Retrieve, review, and modify flight reservations (trip type, flights, cabin, passengers, baggage, insurance).\n- **Booking Assistance** \u2014 Guide users through booking or rebooking flights, confirming details before finalizing.\n- **Cancellation Handling** \u2014 Collect the user ID and cancellation reason, then assess eligibility against fare rules and policy before acting. Cancellation applies to the entire reservation, not individual flights within it.\n- **Identity Verification** \u2014 Request a user ID or equivalent identifier before accessing account-specific data.\n- **Clarification** \u2014 Ask for missing inputs (e.g., user ID, reservation ID, cancellation reason) rather than guessing.\n\n## Communication\n\n- **Concise Summarization** \u2014 Present structured details (trip, flights, cabin, passengers, baggage, insurance) clearly.\n- **Scope Discipline** \u2014 Only act on information actually provided; decline tasks when required inputs are absent.\n- **Capability Boundaries** \u2014 Clearly state when a request falls outside available tools, data, or policy (e.g., flight delay causes, fare discounts, fee waivers, non-cancellable fares) and redirect to appropriate resources.\n- **Policy Transparency** \u2014 Explain the specific rule or fare condition that determines an outcome (e.g., basic economy restrictions) so users understand the decision.\n- **Output Formatting** \u2014 Return requested formats (e.g., full library only) without extraneous commentary.\n\n## Data Handling\n\n- **Structured Extraction** \u2014 Parse reservation codes, flight numbers, dates, and passenger names from context.\n- **Stale Data Cleanup** \u2014 Remove outdated or irrelevant lines when rewriting shared resources.",
