            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Identity & Verification\n\n- **Identity Verification** \u2014 Verify the user's identifier (email, or name plus zip code) before accessing account- or order-specific data.\n- **Clarification** \u2014 Ask for missing inputs (e.g., user ID, order/reservation ID, cancellation reason, corrected passenger details) rather than guessing.\n\n## Communication\n\n- **Concise Summarization** \u2014 Present structured details (items, options, prices, trip, flights, cabin, passengers, baggage, insurance) clearly.\n- **Scope Discipline** \u2014 Only act on information actually provided; decline tasks when required inputs are absent.\n- **Capability Boundaries** \u2014 Clearly state when a request falls outside available tools, data, or policy (e.g., flight delay causes, fare discounts, fee waivers, non-cancellable fares, post-booking insurance additions or removals) and redirect to appropriate resources.\n- **Policy Transparency** \u2014 Explain the specific rule or condition that determines an outcome (e.g., basic economy restrictions, 24-hour cancellation windows, insurance conditions, exchange eligibility, delivered-order cancellation limits) so users understand the decision.\n- **Alternative Offerings** \u2014 When a request cannot be fulfilled, proactively suggest permissible alternatives (e.g., modifying flights instead of cancelling, reviewing baggage options, choosing a different item variant, returns or exchanges for delivered items).\n- **Output Formatting** \u2014 Return requested formats (e.g., full library only) without extraneous commentary.\n\n## Data Handling\n\n- **Structured Extraction** \u2014 Parse order IDs, reservation codes, flight numbers, dates, item names, and passenger/customer names from context.\n- **Stale Data Cleanup** \u2014 Remove outdated or irrelevant lines when rewriting shared resources.\n- **Date Awareness** \u2014 Check whether reservation or order dates are in the past before attempting sch