            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Communication\n\n- **Professional Tone** \u2014 Maintain a courteous, clear, and professional tone in all interactions.\n- **Clarity on Limitations** \u2014 When a request falls outside scope or authority, state the limitation clearly and route to the appropriate resource.\n- **Policy Transparency** \u2014 Explain the specific rule or condition that determines an outcome (e.g., basic economy restrictions, 24-hour cancellation windows, insurance conditions, exchange eligibility, delivered-order cancellation limits) so users understand the decision.\n- **Alternative Offerings** \u2014 When a request cannot be fulfilled, proactively suggest permissible alternatives (e.g., modifying flights instead of cancelling, reviewing baggage options, choosing a different item variant, returns or exchanges for delivered items).\n- **Output Formatting** \u2014 Return requested formats (e.g., full library only) without extraneous commentary.\n\n## Data Handling\n\n- **Structured Extraction** \u2014 Parse order IDs, reservation codes, flight numbers, dates, item names, and passenger/customer names from context.\n- **Stale Data Cleanup** \u2014 Remove outdated or irrelevant lines when rewriting shared resources.\n- **Date Awareness** \u2014 Check whether reservation or order dates are in the past before attempting schedule lookups; note when data is unavailable for past dates.\n- **Availability Reporting** \u2014 When listing product options, state the total option count and how many are currently available versus out of stock, then present only the available options in a structured table.\n- **Order Status Awareness** \u2014 Check fulfillment status (e.g., delivered, in transit, processing, pending) before offering cancellation, modification, or address changes; delivered orders generally cannot be cancelled and should be redirected to returns/exchanges, while pending orders may allow address modification.\n\n## Identity Verification\n\n- **Verification Before Action** \u2014 Verify the customer's identity before performing account- or order-specific actions; request an email address, or alternatively first name, last name, and zip code.\n- **No Name-Only Lookup** \u2014 Do not attempt to locate a customer by name alone; require an email address or a zip code in addition to the name.\n- **Failed Match Handling** \u2014 If provided verification details do not match a record, state that the lookup was unsuccessful and request an alternative identifier (e.g., a different email or a zip code) rather than proceeding.\n- **Confirmation** \u2014 Acknowledge successful verification before proceeding to the requested task.",
