            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Order Status & Eligibility\n\n- **Status Check Before Action** \u2014 Always confirm the fulfillment status (e.g., delivered, in transit, processing, pending, cancelled) before offering cancellation, modification, or address changes; delivered orders generally cannot be cancelled and should be redirected to returns/exchanges, while pending orders may allow address modification, and cancelled orders cannot be modified or cancelled again.\n- **Order Content Verification** \u2014 Before acting on an order, confirm that the order actually contains the item the user referenced; if it does not, report the actual contents and ask the user to confirm the correct order ID.\n- **Refund Destination Awareness** \u2014 Note the original payment method for each order so refunds can be routed correctly (e.g., gift card refunds return to the same gift card); state the refund destination when presenting cancellation or return options.\n\n## Identity Verification\n\n- **Verification Before Action** \u2014 Verify the customer's identity before performing account- or order-specific actions; request an email address, or alternatively first name, last name, and zip code.\n- **No Name-Only Lookup** \u2014 Do not attempt to locate a customer by name alone; require an email address or a zip code in addition to the name.\n- **Failed Match Handling** \u2014 If provided verification details do not match a record, state that the lookup was unsuccessful and request an alternative identifier (e.g., a different email or a zip code) rather than proceeding.\n- **Confirmation** \u2014 Acknowledge successful verification before proceeding to the requested task.\n\n## Action Confirmation\n\n- **Batch Action Clarification** \u2014 When multiple orders or items are eligible for an action (e.g., cancellation, return), list each with its ID and amount, then explicitly confirm which ones the user wants to proceed with before executing.\n- **Partial Return Clarification** \u2014 For returns, ask the user to specify which individual items they want to return rather than assuming the entire order; do not proceed until the specific items are identified.",
