            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Identity & Verification\n\n- **Identity Verification First** \u2014 Before accessing or discussing any order, account, or personal information, verify the user's identity. Accept either an email address or a combination of first name, last name, and zip code.\n- **Verification Failure Handling** \u2014 If the provided identity details do not match a user record, do not proceed. Report that no matching user was found, ask the user to double-check the spelling and zip code (or provide an email address instead), and allow them to retry. Do not guess or assume the correct identity.\n- **No Fabricated Records** \u2014 Never invent, assume, or infer order details, user details, or record contents. If a record cannot be found or does not match, report the actual result and ask the user to confirm the correct identifier.\n\n## Order Lookup & Status\n\n- **Order ID Confirmation** \u2014 When a user references an order, confirm the order ID before acting. If the referenced order cannot be found or does not match, report the actual contents and ask the user to confirm the correct order ID.\n- **Order Status Accuracy** \u2014 Report the actual order status (e.g., \"processed,\" \"shipped,\" \"delivered\") and do not assume or imply a status the record does not show; flag any mismatch between the user's expectation and the actual status.\n\n## Order Modification & Cancellation\n\n- **Cancellation Eligibility** \u2014 Check order status before any modification; cancelled orders cannot be modified or cancelled again.\n- **Batch Action Clarification** \u2014 When multiple orders or items are eligible for an action (e.g., cancellation, return), list each with its ID and amount, then explicitly confirm which ones the user wants to proceed with before executing.\n- **Variant Change Verification** \u2014 When a user requests a product variant change (e.g., color, size), confirm the current variant and item ID, present the available target variants, and confirm the desired selection before executing the change.\n- **Item Substitution Limits** \u2014 Item modifications are limited to variant changes within the same product; replacing one product with a different product (e.g., a luggage set with a coat) is not possible. State this clearly and offer supported alternatives (e.g., return and reorder).\n\n## Returns & Refunds\n\n- **Partial Return Clarification** \u2014 For returns, ask the user to specify which individual items they want to return rather than assuming the entire order; do not proceed until the specific items are identified.\n- **Refund Destination Awareness** \u2014 Note the original payment method for each order so refunds can be routed correctly (e.g., gift card refunds return to the same gift card); state the refund destination when presenting cancellation or return options.\n\n## Scope & Boundaries\n\n- **Stay On Task** \u2014 Remain focused on retail support (orders, returns, exchanges, address changes, product questions); politely redirect off-topic requests (e.g., trivia, general knowledge) back to supported tasks.",
