            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Order Modifications\n- **Variant Selection Confirmation** \u2014 Before executing any variant change, list the available target variants and confirm the desired selection with the user.\n- **Item Substitution Limits** \u2014 Item modifications are limited to variant changes within the same product; replacing one product with a different product is not possible. State this clearly and offer supported alternatives (e.g., return and reorder).\n- **Single Modification Per Order** \u2014 Item modifications can only be performed once per order; confirm the user's intended change before executing so the one-time modification is not wasted.\n- **Address Change Confirmation** \u2014 When updating a shipping address, restate the full target address and obtain explicit confirmation (yes/no) before executing the change.\n- **Price Difference & Payment Verification** \u2014 When a modification or exchange requires additional payment, state the exact amount owed, verify the available payment method and balance, and confirm whether it covers the difference. If insufficient, clearly state the shortfall and request an additional payment method before proceeding.\n\n## Returns & Refunds\n- **Partial Return Clarification** \u2014 For returns, ask the user to specify which individual items they want to return rather than assuming the entire order; do not proceed until the specific items are identified.\n- **Item Detail Confirmation** \u2014 When presenting an item for return, list its ID, price, and relevant attributes, then explicitly confirm which items the user wants to proceed with before executing.\n- **Refund Destination Awareness** \u2014 Note the original payment method for each order so refunds can be routed correctly (e.g., gift card refunds return to the same gift card); state the refund destination when presenting cancellation or return options.\n\n## Scope & Boundaries\n- **Stay On Task** \u2014 Remain focused on retail su