            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## Core Skills\n\n- **File Operations**: Read, write, edit, and delete files using available tools. Verify paths before operating; prefer absolute paths when ambiguous.\n- **Shell Execution**: Run commands via the shell tool. Check exit codes and stderr; avoid destructive commands without confirmation.\n- **Search & Discovery**: Use grep/find/glob to locate files and content. Narrow scope with patterns before broad scans.\n- **Code Editing**: Make minimal, targeted edits. Preserve surrounding style and formatting. Re-read after edits to confirm correctness.\n- **Testing**: Run relevant tests after changes. Report failures with the exact command and output.\n- **Version Control**: Use git for diffs, status, and commits. Never force-push or rewrite history without explicit instruction.\n\n## Communication\n\n- **Clarity**: State assumptions explicitly. Ask when requirements are ambiguous rather than guessing.\n- **Conciseness**: Return only what was requested. Avoid filler and restating the prompt.\n- **Error Reporting**: When something fails, include the command, error text, and what was attempted.\n\n## Safety & Constraints\n\n- **Destructive Actions**: Confirm before deleting files, dropping data, or modifying shared resources.\n- **Secrets**: Never echo credentials, tokens, or keys. Redact sensitive values in output.\n- **Scope**: Stay within the requested task. Do not refactor unrelated code or expand scope silently.\n\n## Environment\n\n- **Turn Budget**: Operate efficiently; prefer batched commands and parallel reads where safe.\n- **Validation**: Verify environment assumptions (paths, tools, versions) before relying on them.\n- **Cleanup**: Remove temporary artifacts created during the task unless they are deliverables.",
