            "carry": "# Shared Skill Library\n\n## File Operations\n\n- **Reading**: Use `cat`, `head`, `tail`, `sed -n` for targeted reads. Prefer line ranges over full dumps for large files.\n- **Writing**: Use heredocs or editors for multi-line content. Confirm write success by re-reading.\n- **Search & Discovery**: Use `grep`, `find`, `glob` to locate files and content. Narrow scope with patterns before broad scans.\n- **Cleanup**: Remove temporary artifacts created during the task unless they are deliverables.\n\n## Code Editing\n\n- Make minimal, targeted edits rather than wholesale rewrites.\n- Preserve existing style, indentation, and conventions.\n- Re-read edited regions to verify correctness.\n\n## Testing & Validation\n\n- Run relevant tests after changes. Report failures with the exact command and output.\n- Verify environment assumptions (paths, tools, versions) before relying on them.\n- Probe for required tools (e.g., `zip`, `tar`, `gzip`) before choosing an approach; fall back to available alternatives (e.g., Python `zipfile`/`tarfile`) when a tool is missing, and state the substitution.\n\n## Version Control\n\n- Use `git` for diffs, status, and commits.\n- Never force-push or rewrite history without explicit instruction.\n\n## Communication\n\n- **Clarity**: State assumptions explicitly. Ask when requirements are ambiguous rather than guessing.\n- **Conciseness**: Return only what was requested. Avoid filler and restating the prompt.\n- **Error Reporting**: When something fails, include the command, error text, and what was attempted.\n\n## Safety & Constraints\n\n- **Destructive Actions**: Confirm before deleting files, dropping data, or modifying shared resources. Treat broad or recursive deletions (e.g., by age, pattern, or directory) as high-risk: enumerate targets first, report scope, and obtain explicit confirmation before executing.\n- **Secrets**: Never echo credentials, tokens, or keys. Redact sensitive values in output.\n- **Scope**: Stay within the requested task. Do not refactor unrelated code or expand scope silently.",
